    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Notion AI better than Grammarly?</h3>
    <p>Notion AI is better for content generation, summarization, and brainstorming inside the Notion workspace. Grammarly is better for grammar checking, tone analysis, and clarity editing across every app you write in. For teams that live in Notion and need first drafts, Notion AI wins. For professionals who write across email, docs, and social media and need polished output, Grammarly wins.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, Notion AI or Grammarly?</h3>
    <p>Notion AI costs $10 per user per month as an add-on to any Notion plan, including the free plan. Grammarly Premium costs $12 per month billed annually, $20 per month billed monthly, or $144 per year. Grammarly also offers a permanent free tier with grammar and spelling checks. If you only need basic grammar checking, Grammarly Free is cheaper. If you need content generation, Notion AI offers more for the price.</p>

    <h3>Can Notion AI check grammar?</h3>
    <p>Notion AI can fix grammar and spelling through its improve writing feature, but it is basic compared to Grammarly. Notion AI catches obvious errors and rewrites sentences for clarity, but it does not provide real-time suggestions, tone analysis, or plagiarism detection. For serious grammar checking across multiple apps, Grammarly is the better choice. For quick fixes inside Notion documents, Notion AI is sufficient.</p>

    <h3>Can Grammarly generate content?</h3>
    <p>Grammarly has a GrammarlyGO feature that can generate drafts, rewrite sentences, and ideate, but it is not as strong as Notion AI for long-form content generation. GrammarlyGO is designed for editing and refinement rather than drafting from scratch. Notion AI is better for generating first drafts, outlines, and summaries because it can reference your Notion workspace content for context.</p>

    <h3>Do Notion AI and Grammarly work together?</h3>
    <p>Yes, and many writers use both. A common workflow is to use Notion AI to generate first drafts, brainstorm ideas, and summarize research inside Notion, then copy the finished draft into Grammarly for final grammar, tone, and clarity polishing before publishing. The combined monthly cost is around $22, which is less than a single hour of professional editing.</p>

    <h3>Which is better for non-native English speakers?</h3>
    <p>Grammarly is better for non-native English speakers. Its real-time grammar, spelling, and tone suggestions work across every app, and its tone detector helps users understand how their writing sounds to native readers. Notion AI can rewrite and improve text, but it does not provide the continuous, surface-level correction that non-native speakers need. For daily writing confidence, Grammarly wins.</p>

